WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:14.297
<v Narrator>Welcome to Once Upon a Time Show. It's time for a bedtime story. Hello, little one. Snuggle down under your blanket, nice and cozy.

2
00:00:14.597 --> 00:00:20.956
<v Narrator>Tonight's story is a very old one. It's one of Aesop's fables, and we tell it in our own words.

3
00:00:21.256 --> 00:00:29.020
<v Narrator>It's about a big, big lion and a tiny, tiny mouse. Who do you think will help whom? Let's find out.

4
00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:35.250
<v Narrator>Once upon a time, in a warm green forest, a great lion lay fast asleep.

5
00:00:35.550 --> 00:00:45.996
<v Narrator>His golden mane was soft and fluffy. His big head rested on his big paws. And he snored, very gently. Rrr. Rrr.

6
00:00:46.296 --> 00:00:55.208
<v Narrator>Nearby lived a little mouse, with round pink ears and a long thin tail. She was small and shy, and she was always in a hurry.

7
00:00:55.508 --> 00:01:01.902
<v Narrator>That day, she was hurrying home, pitter patter, through the tall grass. She didn't look where she was going.

8
00:01:07.202 --> 00:01:11.690
<v Narrator>And whoops! She ran right over the lion's nose. Tickle, tickle!

9
00:01:11.990 --> 00:01:20.474
<v Narrator>The lion opened one big yellow eye. Then the other. And he put his heavy paw down, gently, so the mouse couldn't run away.

10
00:01:20.774 --> 00:01:27.378
<v Narrator>Please let me go, said the little mouse in her tiny voice. If you do, one day I'll help you. I promise.

11
00:01:27.678 --> 00:01:38.467
<v Narrator>The lion smiled. A tiny mouse, helping a great big lion? What a funny idea! But the lion was kind. He lifted his paw, and the mouse scampered home.

12
00:01:44.767 --> 00:01:51.080
<v Narrator>Some days later, the lion was walking through the forest. Suddenly, he stepped into a hunter's net!

13
00:01:51.380 --> 00:01:57.949
<v Narrator>The ropes were thick and strong. The more he wriggled, the tighter they held. He couldn't get free.

14
00:01:58.249 --> 00:02:05.455
<v Narrator>So the lion roared. A big roar that rolled through the whole forest, all the way to the little mouse's home.

15
00:02:05.755 --> 00:02:14.112
<v Narrator>The mouse knew that voice at once. That's my friend the lion, she said. And off she ran, as fast as her little legs could go.

16
00:02:20.412 --> 00:02:25.622
<v Narrator>She found the lion tangled in the net. Don't worry, she said. I'm here.

17
00:02:25.922 --> 00:02:33.175
<v Narrator>She climbed up to one of the great ropes. And with her sharp little teeth she began to nibble. Nibble, nibble, nibble.

18
00:02:33.475 --> 00:02:40.937
<v Narrator>Snap! The rope broke. Then another, and another. And soon the big lion stepped out of the net, free.

19
00:02:41.237 --> 00:02:50.789
<v Narrator>You laughed when I said I would help you, said the mouse. Now you see that even a little mouse can help a lion. And the lion said, thank you, my little friend.

20
00:02:58.089 --> 00:03:05.296
<v Narrator>From that day on, the lion and the mouse were the best of friends. Because a kindness is never wasted.

21
00:03:05.596 --> 00:03:16.205
<v Narrator>And now the forest is quiet. The moon is up, round and silver. The lion curls up under a big tree, and the little mouse snuggles in his soft mane.

22
00:03:16.505 --> 00:03:25.534
<v Narrator>Close your eyes now, little one. Breathe in, breathe out, nice and slow. Goodnight from Once Upon a Time Show. Sweet dreams.
